      "sourceSemantics": "Computes the canonical typed effect-intent digest inside automation, verifies independently signed final-use subject/destination/scope/payload binding with a current dispatch lease before provider entry, appends an immutable provider-attempt row before contact, supports synchronous and async provider-effect drivers with exact wire-payload binding, and composes the optional configured Agentd HTTP execute/reconcile control for already claimed/prepared steps. Version 2 provider keys bind the owning Agent plus TaskFlow run/step under the registered provider scope/destination; stored version 1 attempts retain their historical lookup key. Initial and terminal/proven-absent reconciliation evidence is recorded without blind redispatch; historical exact-attempt observation does not grant new dispatch authority. Generic scheduled-effect/DAG execution and independent host/provider qualification remain separate. New configured HTTP attempts persist an immutable optional provider contract binding before physical dispatch; mismatched remote recovery rejects after local known terminal evidence is settled. Legacy/generic unbound attempts retain their continuity limitations.",
